eans this  giant squid is maybe a subspecies with  certain magical properties  in the harry potter series we know  students love to joke about the giant  squid and sometimes even seem to fear it  a little bit but everything we  know suggests that the giant squid at  least in the harry potter series is  harmless it didn't attack crumb in book  4 when he swam in the lake students were  able to feed it bread on occasion and it  actually even rescued dennis crevey when  he fell into the lake again  in book 4. all right for number six  let's stick with another aquatic  creature here and talk about the kelpie  unlike the giant squid these things are  incredibly  dangerous to humans kelpies are  shape-shifting water demons that are  said to  lurk in rivers and streams they usually  take on the appearance of a horse and  invite humans to  ride across if humans take the kelpie up  on the offer the beast will drag  the writer under and attempt to eat them  yes you heard me right  eat them newt actually managed to tame a  kelpie using a bridle  note to self though should you see a  horse in a river in hogwarts legacy do  not  attempt to ride it at number seven and  rounding out the water creatures for the  list we have the siren  sirens are actually the earliest  recorded race of mer people  in the wizarding world they were  exceptionally beautiful and it's  believed they used their singing voices  to  lure sailors into the water a siren is  depicted on the portrait from the  prefect's bathroom on the fifth  floor of hogwarts this portrait helped  the triwizard champions again book four  specifically cedric diggory in figuring  out the mystery of the golden egg  so even if we don't see an actual siren  in hogwarts legacy i'm definitely  interested to see if the one pictured in  the prefix bathroom makes an appearance  as we're exploring the castle  and at number eight we have the demi  guys a peaceful herbivore with two  insane magical abilities one the power  to become  invisible and two the power to see the  future  because of their pre-cognitive sight  they're insanely hard to catch  their pelts make them highly sought  after though as they're used in making  invisibility cloaks it's said that  cloaks made in this way eventually lose  their effect because the hairs turn  opaque over time you may remember again  newt scamander had a demiguise which  escaped in the middle of new york city  during his trip there in 1926.  at number nine let's talk werewolves of  all the beasts featured on this list i  would say the werewolf is one of the  most well-known throughout  all of harry potter lore thanks in large  part to remus lupin  unlike any other beast on this list  werewolves are of course  partly human there are numerous  variations of the werewolf throughout  popular culture and in the wizarding  world of harry potter they work  mostly in ways that we're familiar with  with the rising of the full moon the  humans suffering from lycanthropy is  transformed into an  uncontrollable wolf with no recollection  of their true identity  it's said a werewolf would even murder  their best friend if given the chance  now they have no control over the  transformation but perhaps most  frighteningly the memories of what they  do in werewolf form will actually remain  with them  when they return to human form should we  see any werewolves in hogwarts legacy  it's safe to say they will be thoroughly  shunned and mistreated by the majority  of the wizarding world  even lupin much later in the timeline  than what hogwarts legacy is said to  take place in  faced prejudice and discrimination in  what we read  we started the list with an incredibly  powerful bird in the phoenix and now  we have another immensely powerful bird  in the thunderbird  these golden and white birds are close  relatives of the phoenix and native to  north america  thunderbirds can actually create storms  around them and they're said to be  highly sensitive to danger  last but not 